            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous aortic laceration causing flail aortic valve and acute aortic regurgitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous laceration of the aorta is an unusual cause of flail aortic valve. We report a case of acute aortic regurgitation caused by flail aortic valve as a result of spontaneous laceration of the ascending aorta. The role of transesophageal echocardiography in the diagnosis of this condition is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
